This program shows a simple menu where the user can pick an option like adding an item, viewing items, opening settings, or exiting. 
It uses if-statements and a nested if inside the settings section to handle different choices. Depending on what the user enters, 
the program prints a message showing what action was selected



This program asks the user to enter three numbers and then uses nested if-statements to figure out which number is the largest.
It compares the numbers step by step and prints the biggest one at the end. 
It’s mainly for practicing conditional logic and comparing values in C++.
